msgid "Nested Dictionaries"
msgstr "Dictionnaires imbriqués"

msgid ""
"Python's built-in :class:`dict` can hold any value — including another "
":class:`dict`. This natural nesting has no dedicated type in the standard"
" library, which makes common tasks (checking whether a key exists "
"anywhere in the hierarchy, counting its occurrences, or converting the "
"whole structure to JSON) unnecessarily verbose."
msgstr ""
"Un :class:`dict` de Python peut contenir n’importe quelle valeur, y "
"compris un autre :class:`dict`. Cette imbrication naturelle n’a pas de "
"type dédié dans la bibliothèque standard, ce qui rend inutilement "
"verbeuses des tâches courantes : vérifier qu’une clé existe à un niveau "
"quelconque de la hiérarchie, compter ses occurrences ou convertir toute "
"la structure en JSON."

msgid ""
"**ndict-tools** fills this gap by providing three ready-to-use classes "
"built on top of :class:`collections.defaultdict`."
msgstr ""
"**ndict-tools** comble ce manque avec trois classes prêtes à l’emploi, "
"construites sur :class:`collections.defaultdict`."

msgid "What is a nested dictionary?"
msgstr "Qu’est-ce qu’un dictionnaire imbriqué ?"

msgid ""
"A nested dictionary is a dictionary whose values may themselves be "
"dictionaries, to any depth:"
msgstr ""
"Un dictionnaire imbriqué est un dictionnaire dont les valeurs peuvent "
"elles-mêmes être des dictionnaires, sur une profondeur quelconque :"

#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
">>> data = {\n"
"...     \"project\": {\n"
"...         \"name\": \"ndict-tools\",\n"
"...         \"version\": \"1.1.0\",\n"
"...         \"authors\": {\n"
"...             \"lead\": \"biface\",\n"
"...         },\n"
"...     },\n"
"...     \"license\": \"MIT\",\n"
"... }"
msgstr ""
">>> data = {\n"
"...     \"project\": {\n"
"...         \"name\": \"ndict-tools\",\n"
"...         \"version\": \"1.1.0\",\n"
"...         \"authors\": {\n"
"...             \"lead\": \"biface\",\n"
"...         },\n"
"...     },\n"
"...     \"license\": \"MIT\",\n"
"... }"

msgid ""
"Accessing ``data[\"project\"][\"authors\"][\"lead\"]`` requires knowing "
"the exact path in advance. With **ndict-tools**, you can also write:"
msgstr ""
"Accéder à ``data[\"project\"][\"authors\"][\"lead\"]`` suppose de "
"connaître le chemin exact à l’avance. Avec **ndict-tools**, vous pouvez "
"aussi écrire :"

msgid ""
">>> from ndict_tools import NestedDictionary\n"
">>> nd = NestedDictionary(data)\n"
">>> nd[[\"project\", \"authors\", \"lead\"]]\n"
"'biface'\n"
">>> nd[[\"license\"]]\n"
"'MIT'"
msgstr ""
">>> from ndict_tools import NestedDictionary\n"
">>> nd = NestedDictionary(data)\n"
">>> nd[[\"project\", \"authors\", \"lead\"]]\n"
"'biface'\n"
">>> nd[[\"license\"]]\n"
"'MIT'"

msgid ""
"The list notation is a *hierarchical key*: each element is a level in the"
" nesting."
msgstr ""
"La notation en liste est une *clé hiérarchique* : chaque élément "
"correspond à un niveau de l’imbrication."

msgid "The three public classes"
msgstr "Les trois classes publiques"

msgid ""
"All three classes accept the same construction patterns — a plain "
":class:`dict`, a :class:`zip`, or a list of ``(key, value)`` pairs:"
msgstr ""
"Les trois classes acceptent les mêmes formes de construction : un "
":class:`dict` simple, un :class:`zip` ou une liste de paires ``(key, "
"value)`` :"

#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
">>> from ndict_tools import NestedDictionary\n"
">>> # From a plain dict\n"
">>> nd = NestedDictionary({\"a\": {\"b\": 1}, \"c\": 2})\n"
">>> nd.to_dict()\n"
"{'a': {'b': 1}, 'c': 2}\n"
">>> # From a zip\n"
">>> nd = NestedDictionary(zip([\"a\", \"b\"], [{\"x\": 1}, 2]))\n"
">>> nd.to_dict()\n"
"{'a': {'x': 1}, 'b': 2}\n"
">>> # From a list of pairs\n"
">>> nd = NestedDictionary([(\"a\", {\"b\": 1}), (\"c\", 2)])\n"
">>> nd.to_dict()\n"
"{'a': {'b': 1}, 'c': 2}"
msgstr ""
">>> from ndict_tools import NestedDictionary\n"
">>> # À partir d’un dict simple\n"
">>> nd = NestedDictionary({\"a\": {\"b\": 1}, \"c\": 2})\n"
">>> nd.to_dict()\n"
"{'a': {'b': 1}, 'c': 2}\n"
">>> # À partir d’un zip\n"
">>> nd = NestedDictionary(zip([\"a\", \"b\"], [{\"x\": 1}, 2]))\n"
">>> nd.to_dict()\n"
"{'a': {'x': 1}, 'b': 2}\n"
">>> # À partir d’une liste de paires\n"
">>> nd = NestedDictionary([(\"a\", {\"b\": 1}), (\"c\", 2)])\n"
">>> nd.to_dict()\n"
"{'a': {'b': 1}, 'c': 2}"

msgid ""
"The difference between the three classes lies in how they respond to an "
"**unknown key**."
msgstr "Les trois classes se distinguent par leur réaction à une **clé inconnue**."

msgid "NestedDictionary — lenient by default"
msgstr "NestedDictionary — permissive par défaut"

msgid ""
"Accessing a missing key silently creates a new, empty "
":class:`~ndict_tools.NestedDictionary` at that location. This mirrors the"
" behaviour of :class:`collections.defaultdict`."
msgstr ""
"Lire une clé absente crée silencieusement, à cet emplacement, un "
":class:`~ndict_tools.NestedDictionary` vide. Ce comportement reprend "
"celui d’un :class:`collections.defaultdict`."

#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
">>> from ndict_tools import NestedDictionary\n"
">>> nd = NestedDictionary({\"a\": 1})\n"
">>> missing = nd[\"missing\"]  # does not raise\n"
">>> type(missing).__name__, len(missing)  # an empty NestedDictionary\n"
"('NestedDictionary', 0)\n"
">>> nd[\"missing\"][\"deeper\"] = 42  # works: intermediate levels are "
"created\n"
">>> nd[[\"missing\", \"deeper\"]]\n"
"42"
msgstr ""
">>> from ndict_tools import NestedDictionary\n"
">>> nd = NestedDictionary({\"a\": 1})\n"
">>> missing = nd[\"missing\"]  # ne lève pas d’exception\n"
">>> type(missing).__name__, len(missing)  # un NestedDictionary vide\n"
"('NestedDictionary', 0)\n"
">>> nd[\"missing\"][\"deeper\"] = 42  # fonctionne : les niveaux "
"intermédiaires sont créés\n"
">>> nd[[\"missing\", \"deeper\"]]\n"
"42"

msgid "StrictNestedDictionary — raises on missing keys"
msgstr "StrictNestedDictionary — lève une exception sur une clé absente"

msgid ""
"Accessing a missing key raises a :class:`KeyError`, just like a plain "
":class:`dict`. Use this class when unknown keys should never go "
"unnoticed."
msgstr ""
"Lire une clé absente lève une :class:`KeyError`, comme avec un "
":class:`dict` simple. Utilisez cette classe lorsqu’aucune clé inconnue ne"
" doit passer inaperçue."

#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
">>> from ndict_tools import StrictNestedDictionary\n"
">>> nd = StrictNestedDictionary({\"a\": 1})\n"
">>> nd[\"missing\"]\n"
"Traceback (most recent call last):\n"
"    ...\n"
"KeyError: 'missing'"
msgstr ""
">>> from ndict_tools import StrictNestedDictionary\n"
">>> nd = StrictNestedDictionary({\"a\": 1})\n"
">>> nd[\"missing\"]\n"
"Traceback (most recent call last):\n"
"    ...\n"
"KeyError: 'missing'"

msgid "SmoothNestedDictionary — always returns a nested dict"
msgstr "SmoothNestedDictionary — renvoie toujours un dictionnaire imbriqué"

msgid ""
"Accessing a missing key returns a new, empty "
":class:`~ndict_tools.SmoothNestedDictionary`. Unlike "
":class:`NestedDictionary`, every returned object is guaranteed to be a "
":class:`SmoothNestedDictionary`, making deep chaining safe regardless of "
"depth."
msgstr ""
"Lire une clé absente renvoie un "
":class:`~ndict_tools.SmoothNestedDictionary` vide. Contrairement à un "
":class:`NestedDictionary`, chaque objet renvoyé est forcément un "
":class:`SmoothNestedDictionary`, si bien que les accès enchaînés restent "
"sûrs quelle que soit la profondeur."

#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
">>> from ndict_tools import SmoothNestedDictionary\n"
">>> nd = SmoothNestedDictionary({\"a\": 1})\n"
">>> result = nd[\"missing\"][\"even\"][\"deeper\"]\n"
">>> type(result).__name__, len(result)  # an empty SmoothNestedDictionary"
"\n"
"('SmoothNestedDictionary', 0)"
msgstr ""
">>> from ndict_tools import SmoothNestedDictionary\n"
">>> nd = SmoothNestedDictionary({\"a\": 1})\n"
">>> result = nd[\"missing\"][\"even\"][\"deeper\"]\n"
">>> type(result).__name__, len(result)  # un SmoothNestedDictionary vide\n"
"('SmoothNestedDictionary', 0)"

msgid "Hierarchical key access"
msgstr "Accès par clé hiérarchique"

msgid ""
"Any :class:`~ndict_tools.NestedDictionary` (and its subclasses) accepts a"
" Python :class:`list` as a key. Reading and writing both work:"
msgstr ""
"Tout :class:`~ndict_tools.NestedDictionary`, comme toute instance de ses "
"sous-classes, accepte une :class:`list` Python comme clé, en lecture "
"comme en écriture :"

#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
">>> from ndict_tools import NestedDictionary\n"
">>> nd = NestedDictionary({\"a\": {\"b\": {\"c\": 42}}})\n"
">>> # Reading\n"
">>> nd[[\"a\", \"b\", \"c\"]]\n"
"42\n"
">>> nd[[\"a\", \"b\"]].to_dict()\n"
"{'c': 42}\n"
">>> # Writing: intermediate levels are created automatically\n"
">>> nd[[\"x\", \"y\", \"z\"]] = 99\n"
">>> nd[\"x\"][\"y\"][\"z\"]\n"
"99\n"
">>> # Deleting: empty parents are cleaned up automatically\n"
">>> del nd[[\"x\", \"y\", \"z\"]]\n"
">>> \"x\" in nd\n"
"False"
msgstr ""
">>> from ndict_tools import NestedDictionary\n"
">>> nd = NestedDictionary({\"a\": {\"b\": {\"c\": 42}}})\n"
">>> # Lecture\n"
">>> nd[[\"a\", \"b\", \"c\"]]\n"
"42\n"
">>> nd[[\"a\", \"b\"]].to_dict()\n"
"{'c': 42}\n"
">>> # Écriture : les niveaux intermédiaires sont créés automatiquement\n"
">>> nd[[\"x\", \"y\", \"z\"]] = 99\n"
">>> nd[\"x\"][\"y\"][\"z\"]\n"
"99\n"
">>> # Suppression : les parents vides sont supprimés automatiquement\n"
">>> del nd[[\"x\", \"y\", \"z\"]]\n"
">>> \"x\" in nd\n"
"False"

msgid "Constructing from an existing dict"
msgstr "Construire à partir d’un dict existant"

msgid ""
"The :meth:`~ndict_tools.NestedDictionary.from_dict` class method provides"
" an alternative constructor that recursively converts a plain dictionary."
msgstr ""
"La méthode de classe :meth:`~ndict_tools.NestedDictionary.from_dict` est "
"un constructeur alternatif qui convertit récursivement un dictionnaire "
"simple."

msgid ""
"A plain :class:`dict` carries no information about how missing keys "
"should behave or how the structure should be printed. As with the "
"constructor, that configuration comes from ``default_setup`` when you "
"give it, and from the default of the class otherwise:"
msgstr ""
"Un :class:`dict` simple n’indique ni comment traiter les clés absentes, "
"ni comment afficher la structure. Comme pour le constructeur, cette "
"configuration vient de ``default_setup`` lorsque vous le fournissez, et "
"sinon de la configuration par défaut de la classe :"

msgid ""
"``indent`` — number of spaces used when printing the dictionary (``0`` "
"disables indentation)."
msgstr ""
"``indent`` — nombre d’espaces utilisés pour afficher le dictionnaire "
"(``0`` désactive l’indentation)."

msgid ""
"``default_factory`` — the class instantiated for missing keys (set to "
"``NestedDictionary`` for lenient behaviour, ``None`` for strict "
"behaviour)."
msgstr ""
"``default_factory`` — la classe instanciée pour les clés absentes "
"(``NestedDictionary`` pour un comportement permissif, ``None`` pour un "
"comportement strict)."

#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
">>> from ndict_tools import NestedDictionary\n"
">>> plain = {\"region\": {\"country\": {\"city\": \"Paris\"}}}\n"
">>> nd = NestedDictionary.from_dict(plain)\n"
">>> nd[[\"region\", \"country\", \"city\"]]\n"
"'Paris'\n"
">>> nd = NestedDictionary.from_dict(\n"
"...     plain,\n"
"...     default_setup={\"indent\": 2, \"default_factory\": "
"NestedDictionary},\n"
"... )\n"
">>> nd.indent\n"
"2"
msgstr ""
">>> from ndict_tools import NestedDictionary\n"
">>> plain = {\"region\": {\"country\": {\"city\": \"Paris\"}}}\n"
">>> nd = NestedDictionary.from_dict(plain)\n"
">>> nd[[\"region\", \"country\", \"city\"]]\n"
"'Paris'\n"
">>> nd = NestedDictionary.from_dict(\n"
"...     plain,\n"
"...     default_setup={\"indent\": 2, \"default_factory\": "
"NestedDictionary},\n"
"... )\n"
">>> nd.indent\n"
"2"

msgid "Searching across all levels"
msgstr "Rechercher à tous les niveaux"

msgid ""
"Because all keys are tracked in the hierarchy, you can search without "
"knowing the depth:"
msgstr ""
"Comme toutes les clés sont suivies dans la hiérarchie, la recherche ne "
"demande pas de connaître la profondeur :"

#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
">>> from ndict_tools import NestedDictionary\n"
">>> nd = NestedDictionary({\n"
"...     \"europe\": {\"france\": {\"capital\": \"Paris\"}},\n"
"...     \"asia\": {\"japan\": {\"capital\": \"Tokyo\"}},\n"
"... })\n"
">>> nd.is_key(\"capital\")  # exists somewhere\n"
"True\n"
">>> nd.occurrences(\"capital\")\n"
"2\n"
">>> nd.key_list(\"capital\")\n"
"[('europe', 'france', 'capital'), ('asia', 'japan', 'capital')]\n"
">>> nd.items_list(\"capital\")\n"
"['Paris', 'Tokyo']"
msgstr ""
">>> from ndict_tools import NestedDictionary\n"
">>> nd = NestedDictionary({\n"
"...     \"europe\": {\"france\": {\"capital\": \"Paris\"}},\n"
"...     \"asia\": {\"japan\": {\"capital\": \"Tokyo\"}},\n"
"... })\n"
">>> nd.is_key(\"capital\")  # existe quelque part\n"
"True\n"
">>> nd.occurrences(\"capital\")\n"
"2\n"
">>> nd.key_list(\"capital\")\n"
"[('europe', 'france', 'capital'), ('asia', 'japan', 'capital')]\n"
">>> nd.items_list(\"capital\")\n"
"['Paris', 'Tokyo']"

msgid "Serialisation"
msgstr "Sérialisation"

msgid ""
"A :class:`~ndict_tools.NestedDictionary` can be saved to and restored "
"from JSON or pickle without any extra setup:"
msgstr ""
"Un :class:`~ndict_tools.NestedDictionary` peut être enregistré en JSON ou"
" avec pickle, puis restauré, sans configuration supplémentaire :"

#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
">>> from ndict_tools import NestedDictionary\n"
">>> nd = NestedDictionary({\"a\": {\"b\": 1}})\n"
">>> # JSON round-trip\n"
">>> nd.to_json(\"nd.json\")\n"
">>> nd2 = NestedDictionary.from_json(\n"
"...     \"nd.json\",\n"
"...     default_setup={\"indent\": 0, \"default_factory\": "
"NestedDictionary},\n"
"... )\n"
">>> nd2.to_dict()\n"
"{'a': {'b': 1}}\n"
">>> # Pickle round-trip (SHA-256 sidecar written automatically)\n"
">>> nd.to_pickle(\"nd.pkl\")\n"
">>> nd3 = NestedDictionary.from_pickle(\"nd.pkl\")\n"
">>> nd3.to_dict()\n"
"{'a': {'b': 1}}"
msgstr ""
">>> from ndict_tools import NestedDictionary\n"
">>> nd = NestedDictionary({\"a\": {\"b\": 1}})\n"
">>> # Aller-retour JSON\n"
">>> nd.to_json(\"nd.json\")\n"
">>> nd2 = NestedDictionary.from_json(\n"
"...     \"nd.json\",\n"
"...     default_setup={\"indent\": 0, \"default_factory\": "
"NestedDictionary},\n"
"... )\n"
">>> nd2.to_dict()\n"
"{'a': {'b': 1}}\n"
">>> # Aller-retour pickle (fichier d’empreinte SHA-256 écrit "
"automatiquement)\n"
">>> nd.to_pickle(\"nd.pkl\")\n"
">>> nd3 = NestedDictionary.from_pickle(\"nd.pkl\")\n"
">>> nd3.to_dict()\n"
"{'a': {'b': 1}}"

